<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Gilde Fund invests 5 mln ECU in Finnish firm.</title>
<headline>Dutch Gilde Fund invests 5 mln ECU in Finnish firm.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch venture capital fund Gilde Buy-Out said on Friday it had invested 5 million ECUs in Finnish firm Metsa Serla Chemicals in which it now hold a stake of almost 10 percent.</p>
<p>The management of Metsa Serla Chemicals and Finnish investment group Industry Kapital will also be shareholders.</p>
<p>Metsa Serla Chemicals is market leader in the production of carbomethylcellulose (CMC), used in the food-, pharmaceutical and detergents industry. The firm produces CMC in Finland, Sweden and the Netherlands.</p>
<p>Dutch Gilde Buy-Out Fund is a unit of Gilde Investment Management in which unlisted Rabobank has a majority stake.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
